-- title:
--   Descent of regularity to the fibre ring S/(varpi)
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring and $\varpi \in A$ an element whose principal ideal $(\varpi)$ is maximal. Let $S$ be a commutative local ring carrying an $A$-algebra structure, and let $K'$ be a field carrying an $A$-algebra structure for which $\varpi$ maps to $0$ in $K'$. Let $B$ be a commutative local ring equipped with an algebra structure over the tensor product $S \otimes_A K'$, flat as a module over $S \otimes_A K'$, and assume that the ring homomorphism $S \to B$ obtained by composing the inclusion $s \mapsto s \otimes 1$ of $S$ into $S \otimes_A K'$ with the structure map $S \otimes_A K' \to B$ is a local homomorphism, i.e. pulls the maximal ideal of $B$ back into the maximal ideal of $S$. Assume further that $B$ is a regular local ring and that its Krull dimension satisfies $\operatorname{dim} B \le 1$. Then the quotient of $S$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ in $S$, that is $S/\varpi S$, is a regular local ring. All four rings are taken in a single universe.
--
--   This is the ring-theoretic form of descent of regularity along a faithfully flat local homomorphism, restricted to targets of Krull dimension at most one (fields and discrete valuation rings): regularity of the geometric fibre $B$ over $S \otimes_A K'$ forces regularity of the fibre ring $S/\varpi S$ below. It is used by the scheme-level statement [`AlgebraicGeometry.isRegularLocalRing_stalk_quotient_span_germ_of_isRegularLocalRing_stalk_pullback_of_ringKrullDim_le_one`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.isRegularLocalRing_stalk_quotient_span_germ_of_isRegularLocalRing_stalk_pullback_of_ringKrullDim_le_one), where $S$ and $B$ are the local rings of a scheme over $A$ and of its base change along $A \to K'$ at a point above.
